      "id": "a1-u02-d07-t01",
      "before": "a1-u02-d07-e01",
      "title": { "en": "Mówić: to speak" },
      "body": { "en": "Mówię, mówisz, mówi. Many verbs go this way: -ę for \"I\", -isz for \"you\", -i for \"he\" and \"she\". At the end of a word, ę is said almost like a plain e." },
      "conjugation": {
        "verb": "mówić",
        "meaning": { "en": "to speak" },
        "forms": { "ja": "mówię", "ty": "mówisz", "on": "mówi", "my": "mówimy", "wy": "mówicie", "oni": "mówią" }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a1-u02-d07-t02",
      "before": "a1-u02-d07-e07",
      "title": { "en": "Po polsku" },
      "body": { "en": "A language you speak is said with po: mówię po polsku is \"I speak Polish\", and po angielsku is \"English\". Trochę means \"a little\" and ale means \"but\". Other languages: po niemiecku (German), po hiszpańsku (Spanish), po francusku (French), po portugalsku (Portuguese)." }
    }
  ],
